the verdict sentencing canadian michael  spavil to 11 years in prison was  delivered behind closed doors in a  courtroom in the northeastern chinese  city of dan dong  the city had been home to the  businessman who organized tours to north  korea until he was detained in december  2018 and charged with sharing state  secrets  former canadian diplomat michael kovrick  was also arrested and charged with  spying both men were tried in march  after more than two years in detention  spawn's sentence was condemned by  canada's ambassador to china  we've maintained from the beginning  that michael spatter and michael kovrig  are being detained arbitrarily and we  will continue to call for their  immediate release  the announcement came as chinese  executive mong won jo faces court in  vancouver in a final push to fight  extradition to the united states  the former huawei chief financial  officer is accused of violating  sanctions on iran  relations between china and canada have  soured considerably  when joe's case is purely politically  motivated these two canadians are  suspected of endangering china's state  security  spava and kovig were detained just weeks  after mung's arrest  ottawa has accused beijing of hostage  diplomacy  canadian prime minister justin trudeau  issued a statement saying the ruling was  unjust and lacked transparency  representatives from 25 countries  including the us uk and japan appeared  at the canadian embassy in beijing in  support of spabo the chinese court  sentenced michael svavo to 11 years in  prison and ordered his deportation but  it's unclear when that would happen  canadian officials say it's most likely  after the jail term is served but some  analysts say it could be sooner an  option used as a bargaining chip with  canada it all hangs on what happens to  miss mung in vancouver and perhaps later  if she is extradited in washington  the verdict follows the upholding of the  death sentence of another canadian  robert schellenberg on tuesday he was  jailed in china in 2014 for drug  smuggling it's unclear when the court  will give its decision on michael  kovrick michael spavy has 10 days to  appeal his sentence but in a country  where 99 percent of criminal cases are  found guilty the chances of overturning  the ruling are unlikely  katrina you al jazeera beijing
 

